#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-vtkAbstractArray-reserve-and-capacity.md:1
msgid ""
"vtkAbstractArray: Deprecate GetSize(), Resize() and Allocate(); Add "
"GetCapacity(), ReserveTuples(), and ReserveValues()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-vtkAbstractArray-reserve-and-capacity.md:3
msgid ""
"The new `GetCapacity()` method in `vtkAbstractArray` clarifies the semantics "
"of VTK array storage. The previous `GetSize()` method was frequently "
"misunderstood, as many users assumed it behaved like `std::vector<T>::"
"size()`, when in fact it reported allocated storage (i.e., capacity). The "
"new naming removes this ambiguity and makes it explicit that the method "
"reflects allocation rather than logical size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-vtkAbstractArray-reserve-and-capacity.md:8
msgid ""
"It should be noted that the `vtkGenericDataArray::Capacity()` which was "
"deprecated in 9.6, has been removed in 9.7, so that the `vtkAbstractArray:"
"Capacity` variable can exist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-vtkAbstractArray-reserve-and-capacity.md:11
msgid ""
"The `vtkGenericDataArray` 's `SetNumberOfTuples()` now behaves like "
"`vtkBitArray`/`vtkStringArray`/`vtkVariantArray` 's `SetNumberOfTuples` "
"which uses `SetNumberOfValues` under the hood, so that data preservation can "
"occur."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-vtkAbstractArray-reserve-and-capacity.md:14
msgid ""
"Similarly, `ReserveTuples(numTuples)` replaces the old `Resize(numTuples)`, "
"whose name suggested behavior analogous to `std::vector<T>::resize()`. In "
"practice, however, `Resize(numTuples)` managed allocated storage rather than "
"logical size and would shrink the allocation when `n` was smaller than the "
"current capacity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-vtkAbstractArray-reserve-and-capacity.md:18
msgid ""
"`ReserveTuples(numTuples)` makes the intent explicit: it adjusts the array’s "
"allocated capacity to `numTuples * numComp` without modifying the logical "
"number of tuples or values. Increasing the allocation is conceptually "
"similar to `std::vector<T>::reserve(n)`. To reduce the logical size and "
"capacity to match the current logical size—behavior analogous to `std::"
"vector<T>::resize(n)` and `std::vector<T>::shrink_to_fit()`—call "
"`SetNumberOfTuples(numTuples)` and `Squeeze()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-vtkAbstractArray-reserve-and-capacity.md:24
msgid ""
"Additionally, `ReserveValues(numValues)` replaces the old "
"`Allocate(numValues)` method, which also managed allocated storage rather "
"than logical size. `Allocate(numValues)` would not preserve existing data. "
"but `ReserveValues(numValues)` will preserve existing data and only increase "
"the allocation if `numValues` exceeds the current capacity. To remove "
"existing data and allocate new storage to match the current logical size-"
"behavior of `std::vector<T>::clear()`, `std::vector<T>::shrink_to_fit()` and "
"`std::vector<T>::reserve(n)`-call `Initialize()` and then "
"`ReserveValues(numValues)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-vtkAbstractArray-reserve-and-capacity.md:31
msgid ""
"Finally, the legacy `GetSize()`, `Resize(numTuples)`, `Allocate(numValues)` "
"methods are now deprecated and will be removed in a future release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-vtkAbstractArray-reserve-and-capacity.md:34
msgid ""
"The same changes have also been applied to `vtkPoints`, `vtkPoints2D` and "
"`vtkIdList`, i.e:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-vtkAbstractArray-reserve-and-capacity.md:36
msgid ""
"`vtkPoints`/`vtkPoints2D`: `SetNumberOfPoints(numPts)` now preserves data, "
"`Reserve(numPts)` replaces the deprecated `Resize(numPts)` and "
"`Allocate(numPts)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/add-vtkAbstractArray-reserve-and-capacity.md:38
msgid ""
"`vtkIdList`: `SetNumberOfIds(numIds)` now preserves data and "
"`Reserve(numIds)` replaces the deprecated `Resize(numIds)` and "
"`Allocate(numIds)`."
msgstr ""
